1
00:02:04,239 --> 00:02:07,699
NO ANIMALS WERE HARMED DURING THE
FILMING OF THIS PRODUCTION

2
00:02:07,699 --> 00:02:20,239
Please contact us for any inquiries
turkision@gmail.com

3
00:02:36,755 --> 00:02:39,805
-Selamun aleykum.
- Alaikum salam, my brother.

4
00:02:40,445 --> 00:02:41,795
You may have a seat.

5
00:02:45,450 --> 00:02:48,150
If you’ll excuse me, I have things to do.

6
00:03:01,479 --> 00:03:03,559
I wanted to talk about Nikola.

7
00:03:04,770 --> 00:03:06,300
I’m listening, brother.

8
00:03:10,513 --> 00:03:12,893
He isn’t the one behind the trap set for
me.

9
00:03:15,907 --> 00:03:17,017
I wanted you to know.

10
00:03:17,434 --> 00:03:20,534
You talk as if you don’t know about the
munition incident.

11
00:03:21,532 --> 00:03:23,612
They were going to destroy everything.

12
00:03:23,920 --> 00:03:27,460
I'm sure he is the one who bribed Yavlak
Arslan’s helper and set the trap.

13
00:03:29,695 --> 00:03:31,695
I didn't say Nikola is innocent.

14
00:03:32,666 --> 00:03:37,206
But I think Yavlak Arslan's helper and
Kuzgun gets support from elsewhere.

15
00:03:45,935 --> 00:03:47,505
Why are you telling me this?

16
00:03:52,400 --> 00:03:53,660
You are the First Alp.

17
00:03:54,925 --> 00:03:56,745
I thought you would take precautions.

18
00:03:58,098 --> 00:03:59,878
Are you trying to lecture me, Osman?

19
00:04:02,004 --> 00:04:03,374
Not at all. (Istighfurullah)

20
00:04:08,285 --> 00:04:09,135
Osman...

21
00:04:12,368 --> 00:04:14,058
Listen to me carefully.

22
00:04:14,058 --> 00:04:14,958
You are a Valiant…

23
00:04:15,808 --> 00:04:16,768
... and brave…

24
00:04:19,266 --> 00:04:20,366
… however…

25
00:04:21,074 --> 00:04:23,494
... not everything you have on your
mind is true.

26
00:04:24,669 --> 00:04:27,769
There were lots of conflicts at the Tent
last year.

27
00:04:28,479 --> 00:04:32,479
I heard that you couldn’t cooperate
with our uncle and Gunduz brother.

28
00:04:33,011 --> 00:04:37,111
Because of you, they got deceived by
our enemies.

29
00:04:41,793 --> 00:04:43,613
What does ‘true’ really mean, brother?

30
00:04:47,807 --> 00:04:49,397
Now that we are at the Tent…

31
00:04:50,929 --> 00:04:53,559
... you can’t make us get deceived by
our enemies...

32
00:04:55,041 --> 00:04:58,681
... just like you did last year.

33
00:05:02,463 --> 00:05:04,343
If it weren’t for me...

34
00:05:07,727 --> 00:05:10,877
... we wouldn’t be making this
conversation at this Tent, brother.

35
00:05:14,004 --> 00:05:17,694
What happens in the past, stays in
the past.

36
00:05:19,196 --> 00:05:21,336
From now on, everyone must know
their place.

37
00:05:21,973 --> 00:05:23,753
When I say stop, you will stop.

38
00:05:23,897 --> 00:05:25,587
When I say walk, you will walk.

39
00:05:26,596 --> 00:05:28,066
And who decides that, brother?

40
00:05:29,120 --> 00:05:30,560
My father, Ertuğrul.

41
00:05:31,135 --> 00:05:33,365
And I, as your big brother.

42
00:05:39,162 --> 00:05:41,572
I see that you got used to our father’s
chair.

43
00:05:46,477 --> 00:05:48,247
And the coat suits you very well.

44
00:05:51,585 --> 00:05:52,485
Very well.

45
00:05:54,725 --> 00:05:55,555
Don’t…

46
00:05:57,863 --> 00:06:00,123
... don’t you accuse me ever again.

47
00:06:02,127 --> 00:06:03,747
I’m not here for the coat.

48
00:06:10,891 --> 00:06:13,041
The things I hear and see are enough
for me.

49
00:06:15,348 --> 00:06:17,498
Who doesn't love the chair and coat?

50
00:06:19,148 --> 00:06:21,358
Those who sat on the chair with ambition…

51
00:06:21,358 --> 00:06:22,968
... left it with disappointments.

52
00:06:25,224 --> 00:06:26,344
Good luck with that.

53
00:06:27,590 --> 00:06:28,860
Remove your hand, brother.

54
00:06:28,945 --> 00:06:30,405
Take your words back.

55
00:06:30,405 --> 00:06:31,925
Remove your hand, brother!

56
00:06:31,925 --> 00:06:33,885
Did I stutter, Osman?

57
00:06:33,940 --> 00:06:35,440
I said remove your hand!

58
00:06:48,398 --> 00:06:50,118
Don’t you ever hit me again!

59
00:06:50,219 --> 00:06:51,209
Know your place!

60
00:06:51,812 --> 00:06:52,982
Take your words back!

61
00:06:52,982 --> 00:06:54,652
I said nothing wrong!

62
00:07:37,229 --> 00:07:39,459
TWO DAYS AGO

63
00:07:42,884 --> 00:07:44,084
What happened here?

64
00:07:45,274 --> 00:07:46,414
Mönke…

65
00:07:47,396 --> 00:07:48,456
What about him?

66
00:07:49,228 --> 00:07:50,748
Mönke…

67
00:07:52,312 --> 00:07:56,142
How on earth, you couln’t handle a
single soldier, Kuzgun!?

68
00:07:57,367 --> 00:07:59,607
You had lots of men with you.

69
00:08:00,343 --> 00:08:02,503
The best soldiers in your service!

70
00:08:02,894 --> 00:08:03,834
Osman…

71
00:08:06,788 --> 00:08:08,408
… he is the devil himself, my Bey.

72
00:08:09,300 --> 00:08:10,320
Devil himself, huh?

73
00:08:10,666 --> 00:08:11,906
You are useless!

74
00:08:18,561 --> 00:08:20,271
What will say to my father, Arslan?

75
00:08:24,126 --> 00:08:26,606
Osman is going to give us everything we
want!

76
00:08:31,233 --> 00:08:31,963
How?

77
00:09:12,777 --> 00:09:14,427
Mönke…

78
00:09:15,680 --> 00:09:17,090
What about him?

79
00:09:17,784 --> 00:09:18,584
Speak!

80
00:09:40,919 --> 00:09:41,709
My Bey!

81
00:09:43,662 --> 00:09:44,942
Come here! It’s important.

82
00:09:47,085 --> 00:09:47,825
Kuzgun.

83
00:09:52,565 --> 00:09:53,675
Be cautious.

84
00:10:11,544 --> 00:10:13,674
It seems they made him pay off.

85
00:10:14,171 --> 00:10:16,521
And it seems they have a
message for you, my Bey.

86
00:10:19,311 --> 00:10:21,551
He who sent this message has left
his mark too.

87
00:10:26,226 --> 00:10:27,406
Let’s see.

88
00:10:36,584 --> 00:10:37,534
It's a trap!

89
00:10:54,447 --> 00:10:55,447
Osman.

90
00:10:55,690 --> 00:10:56,830
Is he dead?

91
00:10:57,009 --> 00:10:59,209
Let’s say his life worths more than his
flesh.

92
00:11:00,790 --> 00:11:01,950
What about Kuzgun?

93
00:11:03,093 --> 00:11:05,013
He is dead as it was necessary.

94
00:11:05,884 --> 00:11:08,914
But his death is going to give us more
Osman's.

95
00:11:10,435 --> 00:11:11,835
You have one last job.

96
00:11:12,178 --> 00:11:13,068
What’s that?

97
00:11:13,916 --> 00:11:16,666
You will go to Konya, to Geyhatu’s
presence.

98
00:11:24,876 --> 00:11:26,656
He will make me worse than deceased.

99
00:11:26,710 --> 00:11:27,630
Don’t worry.

100
00:11:29,088 --> 00:11:31,018
He will treat you with respect.

101
00:11:31,469 --> 00:11:34,539
You will tell Geyhatu about the
fate of his son.

102
00:11:38,021 --> 00:11:39,261
What happened to Mönke?

103
00:11:39,443 --> 00:11:43,443
Osman killed his Nükels and captured him.

104
00:11:43,594 --> 00:11:48,204
He may have killed him by now and fed the
wolves with his corpse.

105
00:11:51,555 --> 00:11:58,355
While you are on your way to Konya, I will
pay a visit to that old wolf.

106
00:12:21,916 --> 00:12:23,736
My Bey, are you okay?

107
00:12:28,614 --> 00:12:30,174
Are you okay, my Bey?

108
00:12:36,574 --> 00:12:37,584
I'm okay.

109
00:13:19,408 --> 00:13:20,658
Any sign?

110
00:13:20,897 --> 00:13:23,997
We've looked everywhere sir but we
couldn’t find anything by now.

111
00:13:24,008 --> 00:13:25,588
As if they are under earth.

112
00:13:29,626 --> 00:13:32,096
They have removed the arrows from the
corpses.

113
00:13:34,407 --> 00:13:36,577
It means they didn’t want to leave any
sign.

114
00:13:38,352 --> 00:13:39,232
The Turks!

115
00:13:39,951 --> 00:13:45,161
Only the Turks have these kind of bows
which can penetrate the bodies this deep.

116
00:13:46,312 --> 00:13:47,682
How did they learn about it?

117
00:13:48,234 --> 00:13:50,374
There is a spy in Castle Inegol.

118
00:13:57,122 --> 00:13:59,562
Once again you did what you do
the best, Ali Chef.

119
00:14:00,566 --> 00:14:02,676
It smells delicious.

120
00:14:04,355 --> 00:14:05,875
My dear father.

121
00:14:10,644 --> 00:14:13,204
Eleftheria, hurry up!

122
00:14:13,366 --> 00:14:15,276
Tekfur Nikola is waiting for his supper.

123
00:14:33,158 --> 00:14:35,828
The new Tekfur is very cautious and
he adores himself.

124
00:14:36,794 --> 00:14:38,514
We must not draw attention.

125
00:14:45,133 --> 00:14:49,583
Mighty Caesar, I’ve been working very hard
ever since I took the office.

126
00:14:50,747 --> 00:14:55,257
And eventually, I’ve made my abawed
people believe in me.

127
00:15:00,823 --> 00:15:04,823
These people, whose ancestors had found
the Roman Empire, became miserable!

128
00:15:04,823 --> 00:15:06,643
Because of their useless leaders!

129
00:15:08,217 --> 00:15:10,147
I’m going to establish a new army.

130
00:15:12,107 --> 00:15:16,667
An army that will take us to the gates
of Jerusalem once again!

131
00:15:29,381 --> 00:15:34,501
So this what the Mongols and Chinese
call flying fire.

132
00:15:35,525 --> 00:15:39,145
I wish we could defeat every scourge
with this.

133
00:15:39,695 --> 00:15:44,275
Be careful, uncle. Nikola probably knows
about the fate of his ammunition by now.

134
00:15:45,078 --> 00:15:46,888
He will do everything to take it back.

135
00:15:47,165 --> 00:15:49,805
Don't worry. I will take every necessary
precaution.

136
00:15:49,805 --> 00:15:53,805
Tell them to be careful and not to get
close it with fire.

137
00:15:56,439 --> 00:15:57,949
Thank you, my nephew.

138
00:15:58,138 --> 00:16:00,198
You saved us all from a big trouble.

139
00:16:00,886 --> 00:16:01,946
Thank you.

140
00:16:03,101 --> 00:16:07,101
If Nikola had this munition…

141
00:16:19,135 --> 00:16:19,955
Nikola…

142
00:16:23,017 --> 00:16:25,367
Caesar is awaiting for your
greetings, Flaetus.

143
00:16:27,229 --> 00:16:28,359
Mighty Caesar.

144
00:16:31,243 --> 00:16:35,493
My old friend, is the flying fire in
my castle?

145
00:16:37,685 --> 00:16:38,685
The Turks…

146
00:16:41,484 --> 00:16:43,904
... they've found the munition and took
it away.

147
00:16:58,152 --> 00:16:59,952
Ertuğrul…

148
00:17:13,950 --> 00:17:19,620
A strong and intelligent enemy makes us
stronger in the end.

149
00:17:22,620 --> 00:17:24,390
Where did they take it?

150
00:17:25,890 --> 00:17:26,980
To Söğüt.

151
00:17:30,236 --> 00:17:34,946
Then it means, the sun will rise at
midnight for Söğüt.

152
00:17:39,606 --> 00:17:44,186
The lights of Heaven will surround
everywhere.

153
00:17:45,954 --> 00:17:48,374
What about the plague I planted into
their seeds?

154
00:17:48,983 --> 00:17:51,873
It kills everyone as we speak and knows
no faith.

155
00:18:00,838 --> 00:18:02,678
I fear it’s the Plague, my Bey.

156
00:18:04,834 --> 00:18:06,254
Plague?

157
00:18:07,208 --> 00:18:08,958
What are you talking about?

158
00:18:08,958 --> 00:18:10,698
It’s killing Söğüt day by day.

159
00:18:11,492 --> 00:18:13,422
As if we don't have enough enemies.

160
00:18:13,422 --> 00:18:15,682
My Rab, may you help us.

161
00:18:17,253 --> 00:18:21,823
We must not get used to losing, Flaetus.

162
00:18:24,210 --> 00:18:29,890
We can’t disappoint our people while they
expect hope from us.

163
00:18:35,788 --> 00:18:38,048
I will take such revenge from the
Turks that...

164
00:18:39,105 --> 00:18:41,545
... they will never dare to take anything
from us.

165
00:18:41,910 --> 00:18:44,080
Do it without leaving any trace.

166
00:18:44,898 --> 00:18:48,268
Don’t let the game of peace we play with
Ertugrul get understood.

167
00:18:50,207 --> 00:18:51,217
For now.

168
00:18:53,095 --> 00:18:54,085
Don’t worry.

169
00:19:27,578 --> 00:19:32,438
You are making yourself sad by thinking
of that imbecile Dündar.

170
00:19:34,637 --> 00:19:36,997
Never in my life, I smiled wholeheartedly.

171
00:19:38,222 --> 00:19:41,762
At least, I can serve my Tent and my
brother.

172
00:19:44,151 --> 00:19:48,621
This sacrifice of yours is going to soothe
us all.

173
00:19:48,658 --> 00:19:49,588
Inshallah.

174
00:19:50,400 --> 00:19:54,400
If one day we make Kayi Tent do what
we say, thanks to you…

175
00:19:54,546 --> 00:19:56,926
... we will become stronger than ever.

176
00:20:04,598 --> 00:20:06,748
Don’t have any doubts, my brother.

177
00:20:07,639 --> 00:20:10,089
Ertugrul is lying on his deathbed.

178
00:20:10,855 --> 00:20:14,095
Because of this, we can’t let go of
Kayi Tent.

179
00:20:14,892 --> 00:20:17,662
I’m ready to do anything.

180
00:20:18,300 --> 00:20:20,540
The power of Kayi has to be ours.

181
00:20:20,820 --> 00:20:22,660
Nobody else’s.

182
00:20:31,820 --> 00:20:34,880
Ertugrul Bey has just invited you to
his presence, Hazal Hatun.

183
00:20:42,062 --> 00:20:43,422
Let's see Valiants.

184
00:20:45,172 --> 00:20:46,582
Who’s going to win?

185
00:20:50,453 --> 00:20:54,263
My Ahmet, throw it with the force of
your arm.

186
00:21:04,895 --> 00:21:06,165
Mashallah.

187
00:21:08,285 --> 00:21:10,955
My dear lions. Go on, continue!

188
00:21:11,816 --> 00:21:13,596
Am I allowed, my Bey?

189
00:21:13,596 --> 00:21:15,036
You may come in.

190
00:21:33,404 --> 00:21:34,454
Little Alps.

191
00:21:34,454 --> 00:21:36,214
Such intelligent children they are.

192
00:21:38,273 --> 00:21:44,413
Just like everybody else who was born
and raised in the Tent of my Ertugrul Bey.

193
00:21:45,371 --> 00:21:46,991
Not at all. (Istighfurullah)

194
00:21:50,770 --> 00:21:55,550
They must learn everything by heart
especially at this age…

195
00:21:55,550 --> 00:22:01,610
... so that they won’t get deceived very
easily when the time comes.

196
00:22:08,966 --> 00:22:10,426
Are you mad at me?

197
00:22:14,354 --> 00:22:16,894
Let’s say I’m rather disappointed.

198
00:22:17,500 --> 00:22:20,070
Perhaps you are disappointed because
of your husband.

199
00:22:21,208 --> 00:22:23,358
He left you and went to Sögut.

200
00:22:25,259 --> 00:22:29,119
Since he left me and went somewhere
many times in the past…

201
00:22:30,209 --> 00:22:32,970
... his infidelity doesn’t hurt me any
longer.

202
00:22:36,276 --> 00:22:37,406
Hooray!

203
00:22:39,814 --> 00:22:41,184
Mashallah!

204
00:22:41,937 --> 00:22:43,737
Ahmet is the winner!

205
00:22:58,094 --> 00:23:02,694
Ever since the Mongols arrived, the coins
are less valuable.

206
00:23:04,381 --> 00:23:07,951
With the help of Allah (Inshallah), you
will able to issue your own coins.

207
00:23:12,239 --> 00:23:13,989
With the help of Allah (Inshallah).

208
00:23:14,379 --> 00:23:16,799
Now, you should train outside.

209
00:23:29,510 --> 00:23:35,050
Hazal Hatun, you better understand that
Ertugrul Bey knows no family…

210
00:23:37,390 --> 00:23:39,700
... when it comes to survival of the Tent.

211
00:23:40,710 --> 00:23:43,930
Our people should also understand this
for the sake of our Law.

212
00:23:48,268 --> 00:23:51,108
Then it means I’m the victim here.

213
00:23:54,507 --> 00:23:57,447
Just like prophet Ishmael became the
victim.

214
00:24:10,383 --> 00:24:12,303
You are free to go.

215
00:24:14,006 --> 00:24:15,526
Thank you.

216
00:24:22,546 --> 00:24:24,046
However...

217
00:24:26,225 --> 00:24:29,095
... the path of your brother is no good.

218
00:24:37,891 --> 00:24:40,181
He either opens his gates to the wrong
people...

219
00:24:40,911 --> 00:24:42,951
... or he is controlled by his ambitions.

220
00:24:46,548 --> 00:24:48,128
You know I like you.

221
00:24:48,906 --> 00:24:50,806
Keep an eye on your brother.

222
00:24:51,177 --> 00:24:53,247
As his sister, you should warn him.

223
00:24:56,367 --> 00:24:58,887
Who am I to warn my brother, my Bey?

224
00:24:59,756 --> 00:25:05,966
But I’d like to know if he has any flaws.

225
00:25:07,297 --> 00:25:11,987
If he says no to his ambitions, everything
will be solved.

226
00:25:49,154 --> 00:25:50,514
Thank you brother.

227
00:25:51,875 --> 00:25:53,855
You endure the pain well, my Bey.

228
00:26:00,959 --> 00:26:03,769
Have some bone broth brother.
It will make you feel better.

229
00:26:06,391 --> 00:26:07,811
I’ve become a burden to you.

230
00:26:13,879 --> 00:26:15,599
These enemies are clever.

231
00:26:17,759 --> 00:26:20,779
They have something to do with
my father’s arrival at the Tent.

232
00:26:22,306 --> 00:26:23,846
What do you mean, my Bey?

233
00:26:25,214 --> 00:26:27,334
Their aim was to kill me.

234
00:26:28,509 --> 00:26:30,059
They want to destroy our Tent.

235
00:26:52,570 --> 00:26:54,260
Selamun aleykum, Alps!

236
00:26:54,317 --> 00:26:55,887
Alaikum selam.

237
00:26:56,313 --> 00:26:57,963
May your night be good.

238
00:26:58,226 --> 00:26:59,886
Welcome, Kumral Abdal.

239
00:26:59,918 --> 00:27:01,238
Please join us.

240
00:27:03,619 --> 00:27:05,439
You’ve already made our night better.

241
00:27:16,497 --> 00:27:17,727
Brother…

242
00:27:19,325 --> 00:27:21,125
... he is a friend of the heart.

243
00:27:21,858 --> 00:27:23,328
I will tell you later.

244
00:27:25,080 --> 00:27:26,040
Welcome.

245
00:27:32,271 --> 00:27:34,511
You worry way too much, Bey’s son.

246
00:27:34,764 --> 00:27:36,734
Some secrets can’t be resolved.

247
00:27:37,510 --> 00:27:39,190
It’s not always easy.

248
00:27:43,578 --> 00:27:45,958
I don’t care about the number of our
enemies.

249
00:27:46,730 --> 00:27:49,050
It’s natural for Valiants to have many
enemies.

250
00:27:49,050 --> 00:27:53,050
However, they wanted to separate me
from my father.

251
00:27:54,372 --> 00:27:56,632
And they knew my father would be at
the Tent.

252
00:27:58,547 --> 00:28:01,137
There is a thin line between knowing and
not knowing.

253
00:28:03,350 --> 00:28:05,020
Solomon knew the language of birds.

254
00:28:05,450 --> 00:28:07,060
He ruled many lands.

255
00:28:07,803 --> 00:28:10,033
Everyone obeyed him.

256
00:28:10,148 --> 00:28:11,658
What happened in the end?

257
00:28:11,658 --> 00:28:13,658
He went to Heaven just like every mortal.

258
00:28:13,658 --> 00:28:15,138
Teshubah!

259
00:28:15,343 --> 00:28:17,453
He who may never die, Bey's son.

260
00:28:20,276 --> 00:28:22,176
Let me tell you what happened.

261
00:28:24,076 --> 00:28:27,916
Solomon who ruled animals, jinns,
people, and who shook the mountains

262
00:28:29,673 --> 00:28:36,813
... once came across to an army of ants
while he was on expedition.

263
00:28:38,074 --> 00:28:43,824
The ants said: “Scatter around! Solomon’s
army is going to crush us all!”

264
00:28:43,824 --> 00:28:45,544
Solomon heard their screams.

265
00:28:46,803 --> 00:28:50,333
Once again the ants said: “Please don’t
crush us and our brothers.”

266
00:28:50,333 --> 00:28:52,163
Who is Solomon not to hear them
scream?

267
00:28:52,293 --> 00:28:54,763
Who is he not to care about the right of
ants?

268
00:28:57,957 --> 00:29:01,357
In the end, that mighty Solomon…

269
00:29:01,357 --> 00:29:02,787
... Valiant Solomon…

270
00:29:03,624 --> 00:29:07,454
... Solomon who cared about the
right of ants...

271
00:29:08,583 --> 00:29:11,213
... ordered his men to change their route.

272
00:29:11,383 --> 00:29:14,013
He cared about even the rights of
simple ants.

273
00:29:14,488 --> 00:29:18,038
This is what true power means: always
caring about one’s rights.

274
00:29:19,800 --> 00:29:21,370
May you be strong.

275
00:29:24,457 --> 00:29:25,527
Please Alps.

276
00:29:25,996 --> 00:29:26,946
Please.

277
00:29:27,615 --> 00:29:31,885
Don’t you ever forget where the power
comes from and why it comes.

278
00:29:33,344 --> 00:29:38,344
Always be conscious enough to hear
the voice of ants.

279
00:29:38,344 --> 00:29:39,674
Amin.

280
00:29:44,597 --> 00:29:45,727
He who may never die.

281
00:29:47,557 --> 00:29:49,047
He who may never die.

282
00:29:50,174 --> 00:29:52,414
The voice of ants and warblers.

283
00:29:52,414 --> 00:29:53,894
The voice of streams.

284
00:29:53,894 --> 00:29:54,984
The voice of horses.

285
00:29:54,984 --> 00:29:57,284
All is nothing but the miracles of our
creator.

286
00:29:58,137 --> 00:30:02,287
He who hurts a life, hurts the creator.

287
00:30:12,516 --> 00:30:14,606
May Allah bless your heart, Kumral Abdal.

288
00:30:28,379 --> 00:30:33,269
It was a silent and peaceful night just
like this one.

289
00:30:35,406 --> 00:30:40,626
The stars surrounded my father and I with
compassion.

290
00:30:41,436 --> 00:30:43,336
The last night I saw my father.

291
00:30:49,774 --> 00:30:55,434
The night, Ertugrul and his Alps sneaked
into Karacahisar Castle.

292
00:30:55,434 --> 00:31:00,114
Sly as a snake, silent as a mouse.

293
00:31:00,114 --> 00:31:03,604
It’s time to revenge that night.

294
00:31:06,220 --> 00:31:09,640
You can no longer take
what’s ours, Ertugrul Bey.

295
00:31:10,418 --> 00:31:11,598
No longer.

296
00:31:19,116 --> 00:31:24,196
May your Ertugrul Bey protect you
from the power of flying fire.

297
00:31:31,311 --> 00:31:33,482
There is going to be chaos in Söğüt
tonight.

298
00:31:33,482 --> 00:31:35,232
Change your uniforms!

299
00:31:35,239 --> 00:31:38,629
Be sneaky and spill it clever to
make your way out of Söğüt.

300
00:31:38,824 --> 00:31:41,104
Fire it and run away.

301
00:31:41,867 --> 00:31:44,047
You are all going to be heroes tonight.

302
00:31:48,999 --> 00:31:51,849
They’ve stored the munition in
the depot, Flaetus.

303
00:31:51,879 --> 00:31:54,119
You’ll revenge your sibling at Heaven.

304
00:31:54,783 --> 00:31:57,073
I don't want to leave it to Heaven.

305
00:31:57,073 --> 00:32:01,743
All I want to do is to be free from the
Turks so that I can open my tavern again.

306
00:32:02,498 --> 00:32:03,438
Soon.

307
00:32:05,020 --> 00:32:07,130
I’ll be your first customer.

308
00:32:14,720 --> 00:32:17,120
This is the twentieth funeral
in Söğüt, my Bey.

309
00:32:30,527 --> 00:32:31,467
Hazal.

310
00:32:40,533 --> 00:32:42,703
My rose and companion.

311
00:32:45,486 --> 00:32:46,746
Hatuns.

312
00:32:48,634 --> 00:32:50,334
They prepared vinegars.

313
00:32:51,337 --> 00:32:52,897
I brought them.

314
00:33:01,203 --> 00:33:06,563
I know that your are mad and dissapointed.

315
00:33:07,633 --> 00:33:12,393
You are sad because I didn’t stop my
brother and left you alone there.

316
00:33:17,377 --> 00:33:19,387
It’s in your nature, Dündar Bey.

317
00:33:20,057 --> 00:33:21,187
In your nature.

318
00:33:23,475 --> 00:33:26,105
However, I know that you are innocent.

319
00:33:26,105 --> 00:33:29,335
If I told you to stop, they would
have thought I was an imposter.

320
00:33:29,335 --> 00:33:32,905
Who was trying to deceive Osman and
I didn’t want to add fuel to flames.

321
00:34:11,520 --> 00:34:12,480
What’s happening?

322
00:34:33,932 --> 00:34:35,592
There is no need to talk.

323
00:34:40,272 --> 00:34:42,112
How’s the situation in Söğut?

324
00:34:44,213 --> 00:34:45,753
Not good.

325
00:34:46,932 --> 00:34:48,812
I closed all the entrances.

326
00:34:50,109 --> 00:34:54,969
I know. I hardly convinced the Alps.

327
00:35:25,413 --> 00:35:28,093
How are you going to feed all these
people?

328
00:35:28,422 --> 00:35:31,822
Alps are carrying food and water to
families.

329
00:35:33,729 --> 00:35:36,599
Hatuns of the Tent should work more
for hours.

330
00:35:37,556 --> 00:35:40,336
It seems things are worse than we think.

331
00:35:57,491 --> 00:35:59,511
Now that you are here…

332
00:36:00,267 --> 00:36:04,267
I will get rid of this plague easily now.

333
00:36:04,515 --> 00:36:07,795
Inshallah. Inshallah.

334
00:36:08,896 --> 00:36:15,076
But, things will get
complicated in the Tent, Dündar Bey.

335
00:36:15,201 --> 00:36:17,261
Keep your eyes open.

336
00:36:17,444 --> 00:36:19,244
Why is that?

337
00:36:21,032 --> 00:36:25,822
I saw the desire of power
in the eyes of Lena and Bala.

338
00:36:34,555 --> 00:36:36,895
They are both ambitious.

339
00:36:37,687 --> 00:36:42,957
They would both give
their lives for their Bey.

340
00:36:44,864 --> 00:36:49,024
And you? Wouldn't you?

341
00:37:09,604 --> 00:37:11,494
Die, you dogs!

342
00:37:12,254 --> 00:37:13,714
Die!

343
00:37:21,806 --> 00:37:24,046
What? What is happening?

344
00:37:32,608 --> 00:37:36,018
Hazal, are you alright?

345
00:37:40,358 --> 00:37:43,658
What is happening?

346
00:37:48,480 --> 00:37:49,840
My Bey!

347
00:37:51,061 --> 00:37:55,061
There were explosions,
we have many casualties!

348
00:37:58,721 --> 00:38:00,321
What are you talking about?

349
00:38:01,178 --> 00:38:02,628
Hazal.

350
00:38:08,961 --> 00:38:10,201
Die!

351
00:38:16,475 --> 00:38:18,655
Rest in peace, father.

352
00:38:19,852 --> 00:38:23,852
Your son, Vladius,
has returned for revenge.

353
00:38:32,580 --> 00:38:34,530
What is it, brother?

354
00:38:38,578 --> 00:38:41,968
I hope it's for the good, brother.
I hope it's for the good.

355
00:38:46,848 --> 00:38:49,348
I saw Söğüt in my dream.

356
00:38:51,791 --> 00:38:54,181
It was blood everywhere.

357
00:38:57,413 --> 00:38:59,823
It was burning.

358
00:40:37,740 --> 00:40:41,100
Cowards attacked while my people
were dealing with the plague.

359
00:40:41,230 --> 00:40:43,790
Those are the ones who
caused this plague, uncle.

360
00:40:43,790 --> 00:40:47,790
You are very smart,
my nephew. Very smart.

361
00:40:48,006 --> 00:40:50,196
- Am I allowed, my Bey?
- What is it, Saltuk?

362
00:40:50,318 --> 00:40:51,934
A man says "It came."

363
00:40:51,934 --> 00:40:54,784
Come on, don't keep me busy for nonsense!

364
00:40:54,878 --> 00:40:57,528
Stop, uncle. It's important.

365
00:41:04,980 --> 00:41:06,620
Can I come in, my Bey?

366
00:41:07,201 --> 00:41:08,491
Come.

367
00:41:20,847 --> 00:41:25,007
We have... so many casualties, my Bey.

368
00:41:28,597 --> 00:41:30,697
Tell Dündar Bey...

369
00:41:31,507 --> 00:41:35,107
... to take care of the
ones who got hurt...

370
00:41:36,270 --> 00:41:43,140
... to rebuild everywhere that's
been damaged, destroyed...

371
00:41:43,846 --> 00:41:47,846
... and pay for every
expense of the ones...

372
00:41:48,553 --> 00:41:54,153
... who have lost their parents,
both the Muslims, and non-Muslims.

373
00:41:58,747 --> 00:42:00,687
By your orders, my Bey.

374
00:42:37,140 --> 00:42:39,430
That Vladius coward did it.

375
00:42:40,266 --> 00:42:42,626
Names of Vladius' men.

376
00:43:05,519 --> 00:43:10,599
With these drawings, I will prepare such
a celebration for them in the castle...

377
00:43:10,599 --> 00:43:14,599
Nephew, what would
my brother say for this?

378
00:43:15,026 --> 00:43:17,226
We have ashamed my father, uncle!

379
00:43:18,161 --> 00:43:20,951
I can not see my father
without ending this!

380
00:43:21,457 --> 00:43:25,977
May seeing my father be forbidden to
me until I take our revenge for this!

381
00:43:52,159 --> 00:43:56,099
He hasn't been around for a
long time, I hope it's not bad news.

382
00:44:18,970 --> 00:44:23,400
Welcome, my Bey. I hope you liked
the goods you bought last time.

383
00:44:23,400 --> 00:44:27,040
Thank you, you should
prepare a chestful of more.

384
00:44:27,606 --> 00:44:29,356
By your command, my Bey.

385
00:45:01,489 --> 00:45:03,279
Can I come in?

386
00:45:06,381 --> 00:45:07,671
Come.

387
00:45:14,803 --> 00:45:18,113
-Salaimun Alaikum.
-Alaikum Salam.

388
00:45:19,645 --> 00:45:25,355
You're late son. We were waiting for you.
Where were you, what were you doing?

389
00:45:25,969 --> 00:45:29,969
Ertuğrul Bey. You came
to me and asked questions.

390
00:45:30,393 --> 00:45:32,433
Now, I came to you and you ask again.

391
00:45:32,967 --> 00:45:35,987
If this is special for me, I am flattered.

392
00:45:35,987 --> 00:45:41,037
But, if you treat everyone
like this, I would be sad.

393
00:45:42,152 --> 00:45:46,942
Because I would say " We weren't special
in the eyes of Ertuğrul Bey after all."

394
00:45:49,469 --> 00:45:52,639
Are you hungry?
Should we set a table for you?

395
00:45:53,970 --> 00:45:56,350
I came to see my sister Hazal.

396
00:45:57,424 --> 00:45:59,854
And I decided to take her with me.

397
00:46:01,576 --> 00:46:03,246
Her husband is Dündar.

398
00:46:04,580 --> 00:46:11,110
Without his permission,
you can't even take her clothes!

399
00:46:13,990 --> 00:46:16,970
No problem. Then we'll spill blood.

400
00:46:20,971 --> 00:46:26,201
Bay Sungur, bring a chicken,
Yavlak Arslan will spill blood.

401
00:46:30,657 --> 00:46:34,997
You can only cut a chicken in our Tent!

402
00:46:54,197 --> 00:47:01,767
Osman Bey is coming!

403
00:47:11,253 --> 00:47:14,283
May I die for your Allah! Look at you!

404
00:47:19,637 --> 00:47:23,637
Thank Allah for this reunion!

405
00:47:23,825 --> 00:47:27,085
What happened? Who set this trap?

406
00:47:29,584 --> 00:47:31,214
Did you take lives?

407
00:47:31,445 --> 00:47:34,105
Calm down, master Davut,
we will tell everything.

408
00:47:42,881 --> 00:47:45,691
Yavlak Arslan is the guest of our Bey.

409
00:47:59,354 --> 00:48:03,354
Your father was a Ghazi. A good one.

410
00:48:04,261 --> 00:48:07,601
Because he wouldn't turn
to the Turkmen Tents...

411
00:48:08,088 --> 00:48:10,198
... he would attack the enemy.

412
00:48:11,531 --> 00:48:18,091
In which house you grew in, that you are
talking about spilling brothers' blood?

413
00:48:18,327 --> 00:48:21,567
We would die for our
brothers if necessary.

414
00:48:21,721 --> 00:48:28,201
But only if they look after their
entrusted, if they don't hurt them.

415
00:48:35,037 --> 00:48:37,027
Osman Bey is here, my Bey.

416
00:48:48,198 --> 00:48:54,458
Be Hazal's guest for a while,
I will fulfill my longing for my son.

417
00:48:56,225 --> 00:48:58,455
Then we'll talk.

418
00:49:08,127 --> 00:49:11,797
My Bey, thank Allah
for your safe return.

419
00:49:12,234 --> 00:49:13,594
My Bala.

420
00:49:23,420 --> 00:49:27,140
Now, if you'll excuse me,
I will see my father.

421
00:49:48,275 --> 00:49:49,905
Salaimun Alaikum.

422
00:49:52,389 --> 00:49:54,269
Alaikum Salam, Arslan Bey.

423
00:49:54,841 --> 00:50:01,211
I am sorry to hear about it, Osman.
A dog in our doors ashamed us all.

424
00:50:02,952 --> 00:50:06,192
We have time to talk
about these, Arslan Bey.

425
00:51:09,959 --> 00:51:11,129
Father.

426
00:51:15,865 --> 00:51:16,915
Father.

427
00:51:54,862 --> 00:51:56,922
I would die for you, my father.

428
00:51:58,988 --> 00:52:00,408
You came.

429
00:52:03,001 --> 00:52:04,511
I saw you.

430
00:52:07,591 --> 00:52:15,411
Thank Allah.

431
00:52:21,622 --> 00:52:23,412
Thank Allah.

432
00:52:25,414 --> 00:52:27,004
Thank Allah.

433
00:52:38,396 --> 00:52:43,386
I pass through many flames in your way.

434
00:52:44,842 --> 00:52:47,052
I pass, but I am not hurt.

435
00:52:49,857 --> 00:52:51,847
For I come to you, father.

436
00:52:52,118 --> 00:52:55,298
I know, son. I know.

437
00:52:57,041 --> 00:53:01,721
If you hadn't come,
our summer would be winter.

438
00:53:02,928 --> 00:53:05,508
If something had happened to you...

439
00:53:06,907 --> 00:53:10,907
My rage would be like
thunderstorms in all the world.

440
00:53:11,908 --> 00:53:13,978
Know that.

441
00:53:14,653 --> 00:53:18,883
I know, father. I know.

442
00:53:20,579 --> 00:53:26,859
With Allah's permission, we will make
many tyrants bow under this banner.

443
00:53:29,189 --> 00:53:31,199
I know that too.

444
00:53:31,199 --> 00:53:34,799
Thank Allah for this reunion.

445
00:53:36,134 --> 00:53:38,144
Thank Allah for this reunion.

446
00:53:39,249 --> 00:53:41,239
Thank Allah for this reunion.

447
00:54:12,959 --> 00:54:17,679
Ertuğrul Bey gave people a lesson with me.

448
00:54:18,090 --> 00:54:22,950
He is a Bey. He gives
lessons, he cuts heads.

449
00:54:23,674 --> 00:54:27,124
But he can't do that to us, sister!

450
00:54:29,171 --> 00:54:32,201
I forgave his imbecile
brother and came here.

451
00:54:32,390 --> 00:54:35,790
Look what they've done,
instead of being thankful.

452
00:54:44,389 --> 00:54:45,689
Brother.

453
00:54:49,293 --> 00:54:52,033
You set the trap on Osman, right?

454
00:54:53,467 --> 00:54:55,557
My smart sister.

455
00:54:56,152 --> 00:55:00,152
Let's call that,
reminding him his place.

456
00:55:02,530 --> 00:55:04,870
Scratching his fame.

457
00:55:08,683 --> 00:55:12,133
No one could surpass me in Turkmen lands.

458
00:55:14,166 --> 00:55:17,436
That's certain. But...

459
00:55:17,909 --> 00:55:20,899
... if they find out you did this-

460
00:55:21,114 --> 00:55:27,724
Hazal, if I am stupid enough
to fall into my own trap...

461
00:55:27,902 --> 00:55:34,952
... may the milk of my mother be haram,
may the sword of my father find me!

462
00:55:44,206 --> 00:55:46,596
What is my place in this, brother?

463
00:55:47,797 --> 00:55:52,317
They won't give up on this, sister.

464
00:55:52,996 --> 00:55:57,756
Keep your eyes open, every
information is precious to me.

465
00:56:02,341 --> 00:56:07,591
Sister, walk on snow,
but hide your tracks.

466
00:56:10,757 --> 00:56:15,517
They wanted to kill me. Kuzgun
took refuge in Mongols.

467
00:56:16,776 --> 00:56:20,126
They set a trap inside of a trap.

468
00:56:20,586 --> 00:56:22,596
That is devil's nature!

469
00:56:25,627 --> 00:56:27,377
Who could've done this, my Bey?

470
00:56:29,040 --> 00:56:31,530
Yavlak Arslan could be in this.

471
00:56:33,685 --> 00:56:37,685
We will watch, we will see.

472
00:56:39,175 --> 00:56:41,795
When the time comes, we will understand.

473
00:56:44,399 --> 00:56:46,059
Can I come in?

474
00:56:47,041 --> 00:56:48,191
Come.

475
00:56:59,308 --> 00:57:03,308
-Salaimun Alaikum.
-Alaikum Salam.

476
00:57:13,007 --> 00:57:16,597
Alaikum Salam.

477
00:57:19,308 --> 00:57:21,268
Come, Arslan Bey.

478
00:57:40,009 --> 00:57:42,949
My Osman, I am sorry for you, again.

479
00:57:46,608 --> 00:57:48,368
Thank you.

480
00:57:52,469 --> 00:57:58,769
I came, for it troubles me. They want
us to fight within ourselves.

481
00:58:01,710 --> 00:58:04,190
Would the devil's game ever end?

482
00:58:05,611 --> 00:58:08,041
It will continue until the end.

483
00:58:12,760 --> 00:58:18,070
Kuzgun... Have you seen
anything about that Kuzgun dog?

484
00:58:18,313 --> 00:58:21,763
I sent all my soldiers after that dog.

485
00:58:23,500 --> 00:58:25,940
He was in Mongolian headquarters.

486
00:58:26,678 --> 00:58:27,838
But...

487
00:58:30,133 --> 00:58:32,243
Someone removed the tracks.

488
00:58:33,778 --> 00:58:36,558
Of course they did, Osman.

489
00:58:38,227 --> 00:58:42,227
The ones who set the trap,
can also remove the tracks.

490
00:58:42,968 --> 00:58:47,758
But, haven't you seen anything?

491
00:58:49,519 --> 00:58:53,519
Beys. Neither the devil...

492
00:58:54,500 --> 00:58:56,590
... nor the good ones will stop.

493
00:58:58,979 --> 00:59:05,649
Arslan, you came, you said you don't know
about it. We believe you. Thank you.

494
00:59:06,281 --> 00:59:13,141
Not only Osman, if anyone from your
Tent gets hurt, my heart would burn.

495
00:59:16,533 --> 00:59:18,423
Thank you.

496
00:59:26,576 --> 00:59:28,406
My road is long.

497
00:59:29,830 --> 00:59:31,520
If you'll excuse me.

498
01:00:39,735 --> 01:00:40,995
Osman!

499
01:00:53,382 --> 01:00:54,992
Osman!

500
01:00:56,514 --> 01:00:57,984
My Bala!

501
01:01:26,403 --> 01:01:28,553
You were gone, I was no more.

502
01:01:32,939 --> 01:01:35,329
I came, I've found life.

503
01:01:38,788 --> 01:01:42,648
My heart bled, my tongue went silent.

504
01:01:42,843 --> 01:01:46,843
I got hurt, you were my hope.

505
01:02:02,042 --> 01:02:04,042
What is it?

506
01:02:07,641 --> 01:02:11,641
Bring a pot. Bring a pot.

507
01:03:30,443 --> 01:03:34,513
No water, brother Dumrul.
Yet you are still dirty.

508
01:03:35,281 --> 01:03:37,821
You talk more than you help.

509
01:03:57,884 --> 01:03:59,464
Brother Boran?

510
01:03:59,464 --> 01:04:02,064
Here we go...

511
01:04:06,248 --> 01:04:10,598
I have some business, brothers,
I should get going.

512
01:04:10,598 --> 01:04:14,228
Brother, do everything,
but don't do this to us.

513
01:04:14,611 --> 01:04:16,441
We would notice.

514
01:04:18,893 --> 01:04:21,093
What? What did you notice?

515
01:04:21,093 --> 01:04:23,033
Don't think us for idiots.

516
01:04:23,311 --> 01:04:29,371
What would you say, if Osman Bey sees you
like this and says "Is there a wedding?"

517
01:04:30,244 --> 01:04:37,014
Even the chickens in the Tent would
understand your intentions from your look.

518
01:04:41,654 --> 01:04:47,114
What did my Bamsı Bey say? Leave no trace.

519
01:04:51,404 --> 01:04:55,884
Thank you, you are right, brothers.

520
01:05:27,463 --> 01:05:29,263
Thank you, brothers.

521
01:05:44,441 --> 01:05:46,811
Your brother, Savcı has returned too.

522
01:05:47,531 --> 01:05:49,491
Really, my Bala?

523
01:05:57,056 --> 01:05:59,856
We even forgot our brother in all this.

524
01:06:00,921 --> 01:06:03,101
It has been many years.

525
01:06:04,482 --> 01:06:06,722
I haven't seen him in a long time.

526
01:06:07,359 --> 01:06:09,679
My father sent him to Crimea last time.

527
01:06:12,798 --> 01:06:15,718
Lena helped us very much.

528
01:06:15,772 --> 01:06:17,672
Of course she did.

529
01:06:20,110 --> 01:06:25,270
Thank Allah, our family
is being whole again.

530
01:06:30,604 --> 01:06:31,814
By the way...

531
01:06:33,370 --> 01:06:36,700
... your Alp, Boran,
is in love with Gonca.

532
01:06:41,553 --> 01:06:47,703
Then tell your companion to not
be so hard on my Boran like you did.

533
01:06:48,415 --> 01:06:52,605
We are Âhi women. Is that so easy to
conquer our hearts, Osman Bey?

534
01:06:52,947 --> 01:06:57,727
I have experience because of you.
I will tell Boran to take caution.

535
01:06:59,027 --> 01:07:02,327
I already trained Gonca for this.

536
01:07:47,216 --> 01:07:48,436
Salaimun Alaikum.

537
01:07:50,455 --> 01:07:51,975
Alaikum Salam.

538
01:07:53,860 --> 01:07:55,350
Was it you?

539
01:07:56,627 --> 01:07:58,177
Thank you.

540
01:08:02,136 --> 01:08:05,586
She is stubborn, she won't give her milk.

541
01:08:06,005 --> 01:08:08,155
If you don't know how to take it...

542
01:08:09,474 --> 01:08:11,134
Is that so?

543
01:08:12,949 --> 01:08:16,159
Come, then, take it yourself.

544
01:08:16,390 --> 01:08:20,760
I won't, it's a woman's job.

545
01:08:21,026 --> 01:08:25,026
Then, don't talk like you know about it.

546
01:08:28,057 --> 01:08:32,057
If I take it, would you
race horses with me?

547
01:08:41,103 --> 01:08:43,393
You won't be able to anyway.

548
01:08:43,816 --> 01:08:44,956
Come.

549
01:09:11,092 --> 01:09:13,222
Don't fail me, please.

550
01:09:13,638 --> 01:09:16,228
Come on, Bismillahirrahmanirrahim.

551
01:09:26,401 --> 01:09:28,591
Hey Mashallah!

552
01:09:50,122 --> 01:09:52,252
Hey Mashallah!

553
01:09:53,475 --> 01:09:55,185
Hey Mashallah!

554
01:10:14,834 --> 01:10:16,274
Thank you.

555
01:10:17,497 --> 01:10:21,497
We will race in Yeşilpınar,
you should come.

556
01:11:05,400 --> 01:11:06,786
Brother!

557
01:11:07,736 --> 01:11:09,169
Brother?

558
01:11:11,908 --> 01:11:15,193
-Mashallah!
-My lion!

559
01:11:19,818 --> 01:11:23,214
It's been a long while.
Thank Allah for this reunion.

560
01:11:23,449 --> 01:11:25,488
Thank Allah, indeed.

561
01:11:26,023 --> 01:11:28,283
Who was behind the ambush?

562
01:11:28,795 --> 01:11:32,552
We couldn't find a mark, brother.

563
01:11:34,042 --> 01:11:36,261
Did you come without a track from the hunt?

564
01:11:37,061 --> 01:11:40,546
This is a hunt, brother.
We were unlucky.

565
01:11:42,263 --> 01:11:46,782
I will reveal the one who ambushed
you and the ones who move against us.

566
01:11:48,544 --> 01:11:51,608
Inshallah, brother. Inshallah.

567
01:11:53,487 --> 01:11:55,925
Well, there was a raid at Söğüt?

568
01:11:56,681 --> 01:11:59,814
Weasel Nicola tried to take revenge.

569
01:12:00,244 --> 01:12:03,073
But I will give him the real hell.

570
01:12:03,852 --> 01:12:07,807
I wonder what's on your mind, brother.
I want to help.

571
01:12:08,919 --> 01:12:14,600
Get rest, my valiant. And don't abstract
yourself with these matters.

572
01:12:16,234 --> 01:12:19,927
Your brother is here,
enjoy yourself.

573
01:12:21,924 --> 01:12:25,909
What do you mean by enjoying, brother?
Aren't we here for each other?

574
01:12:26,056 --> 01:12:30,758
You are wayworn, brother.
If I say don't worry, then don't worry.

575
01:13:17,427 --> 01:13:19,082
Look here!

576
01:13:20,200 --> 01:13:22,221
We are facing the enemy, the enemy!

577
01:13:22,957 --> 01:13:25,902
What is this slackness?
What is this frailness?

578
01:13:27,196 --> 01:13:28,468
Get up!

579
01:13:36,866 --> 01:13:38,123
Attack!

580
01:13:48,868 --> 01:13:51,132
If you fall, the army falls!

581
01:13:52,891 --> 01:13:54,015
Get up!

582
01:13:55,296 --> 01:13:58,584
One for all, all for one!

583
01:14:01,278 --> 01:14:05,780
If you fall, you die!
If you die, we lose our army!

584
01:14:18,398 --> 01:14:20,013
Come on, come on!

585
01:14:30,353 --> 01:14:32,014
Welcome, my bey.

586
01:14:37,960 --> 01:14:39,782
In an army...

587
01:14:42,816 --> 01:14:45,077
...love is as important as fear.

588
01:14:48,845 --> 01:14:51,627
-Do you know for what?
-For battle, my bey.

589
01:14:53,699 --> 01:14:55,373
No.

590
01:14:56,573 --> 01:14:58,640
For their commander.

591
01:14:59,231 --> 01:15:04,847
They shouldn't fear their commander,
they should love him to death.

592
01:15:05,261 --> 01:15:10,996
They should love so that they can run
to die when ordered to.

593
01:15:20,207 --> 01:15:22,566
They aren't the Mongol army...

594
01:15:24,052 --> 01:15:28,420
...and you aren't a Mongol warrior now.

595
01:15:30,077 --> 01:15:32,363
Don't forget that.

596
01:15:41,681 --> 01:15:44,408
Thank you, my bey.
May you live long.

597
01:15:48,998 --> 01:15:52,047
For you, I will train an army that is ready
to die.

598
01:15:53,986 --> 01:15:55,756
It will be such an army that...

599
01:15:56,980 --> 01:15:59,660
...it will bring the Turk-Islam order
to the world.

600
01:16:15,149 --> 01:16:17,068
Osman Bey.

601
01:17:40,877 --> 01:17:43,543
I can take care of the rest.
Mind your business.

602
01:19:00,842 --> 01:19:04,610
-These drinkers over there.
-Thank you, Zülfikar Dervish.

603
01:19:36,060 --> 01:19:37,507
My Bey.

604
01:19:38,805 --> 01:19:40,902
What makes you think?

605
01:19:42,250 --> 01:19:45,369
I'm eating my heart out, Bala.
I'm eating my heart out.

606
01:19:45,977 --> 01:19:49,802
The enemy is strong and so should we.

607
01:19:51,730 --> 01:19:54,362
We need to strengthen the army.

608
01:19:55,054 --> 01:19:58,424
If my brother Gündüz gets appointed
to Kuluca Hisar...

609
01:19:59,072 --> 01:20:01,858
...and I get tasked by the
reformation of the army...

610
01:20:02,765 --> 01:20:04,787
...then...

611
01:20:06,987 --> 01:20:09,008
May I enter, Osman Bey.

612
01:20:15,441 --> 01:20:17,068
I'm coming, my Bey.

613
01:20:30,643 --> 01:20:34,591
What do you mean my Bey?
Of course, you can enter.

614
01:20:41,092 --> 01:20:44,842
You are the Bey of where your
wife is.

615
01:20:48,089 --> 01:20:49,897
Of course, I will ask.

616
01:20:57,696 --> 01:20:59,761
Help yourself, father.

617
01:21:01,753 --> 01:21:04,069
The dinner is ready, Ertuğrul Bey.

618
01:21:05,638 --> 01:21:07,599
Thank you, my girl.

619
01:21:17,386 --> 01:21:19,184
If you allow me.

620
01:21:27,722 --> 01:21:29,920
With the name of Allah.

621
01:21:34,888 --> 01:21:36,723
With the name of Allah.

622
01:21:47,401 --> 01:21:51,467
Tell me, Osman Bey.
What is the situation at the Tents?

623
01:21:53,580 --> 01:21:57,324
Do the trees comply with their leaves?
The sheep with their lambs?

624
01:21:58,776 --> 01:22:01,718
Brothers with brothers?

625
01:22:03,447 --> 01:22:06,703
The trees are pleased with their fruits,
the sheep with their milk...

626
01:22:06,703 --> 01:22:11,915
...and brothers with their brothers,
my bey. Thank Allah.

627
01:22:13,258 --> 01:22:16,213
So, what's the situation of our Alps?

628
01:22:16,762 --> 01:22:22,218
Our Alps are heroes. In a short time,
they became as capable as a swordmaster.

629
01:22:22,855 --> 01:22:27,539
Our archers reached longest ranges of
the last five years. Our horses...

630
01:22:27,539 --> 01:22:32,146
...are stronger than before, even faster.
-What is the situation of our equipment?

631
01:22:32,651 --> 01:22:37,380
We have the arrows to pierce the
tyrants. The weapons to arm the innocent.

632
01:22:38,945 --> 01:22:44,460
The sharpness of a weapon won't matter
to the plays of the enemy, son.

633
01:22:45,012 --> 01:22:49,438
We will overcome with our minds,
destroy their games with our hands, father.

634
01:22:51,216 --> 01:22:52,811
But...

635
01:22:55,703 --> 01:22:57,444
Go on, but?

636
01:22:58,976 --> 01:23:02,828
My Bey, what we lack is fire.

637
01:23:03,635 --> 01:23:07,870
Our Alps need to warm up for
victories.

638
01:23:10,519 --> 01:23:12,420
If you allow it...

639
01:23:13,201 --> 01:23:16,037
...I want to be responsible for the
recovery of the army--

640
01:23:17,387 --> 01:23:19,955
Every Alp will fight their own battle,
son.

641
01:23:21,923 --> 01:23:25,043
After not being able to control their
conceit, wroth...

642
01:23:27,847 --> 01:23:30,965
...even if they have the fire,
what they will burn is certain.

643
01:23:33,083 --> 01:23:36,716
Victory belongs to ones who are
afraid to defy Allah's orders.

644
01:23:48,050 --> 01:23:50,842
Three of you, prowl around.
You, come with me.

645
01:24:13,877 --> 01:24:15,911
Enjoy it.

646
01:24:33,899 --> 01:24:37,232
-Drink some of our holy water.
-Thank you, my monk.

647
01:24:37,250 --> 01:24:40,740
This is our best day.
To our victory!

648
01:24:48,238 --> 01:24:50,990
To reascension of the Byzantines!

649
01:25:09,816 --> 01:25:13,075
Didn't I tell you to not drink that much?

650
01:25:48,613 --> 01:25:51,808
Oh, Lena Hatun.
Let's finish this vinegar.

651
01:26:07,341 --> 01:26:10,504
-Haven't anyone told you?
-Told me what?

652
01:26:11,531 --> 01:26:14,894
That I'm an Orthodox Christian.

653
01:26:15,274 --> 01:26:16,543
No.

654
01:26:19,556 --> 01:26:24,466
This is why I loved Savcı Bey.
This is why I married him.

655
01:26:25,604 --> 01:26:28,149
Who is who doesn't matter to him.

656
01:26:30,681 --> 01:26:34,164
-How did you meet with brother Savcı?
-At Karacahisar.

657
01:26:36,362 --> 01:26:39,231
Before Ertuğrul Bey conquered our castle.

658
01:26:42,056 --> 01:26:47,993
My father was working for a wealthy noble.
He was a good navvy. He was working all day.

659
01:26:51,021 --> 01:26:54,109
One day, when they were taking
the goods to the city...

660
01:26:54,698 --> 01:26:58,574
...the cart topples down with
the goods.

661
01:27:00,324 --> 01:27:04,357
The seigneur gets too mad and
he does cruelty to my father.

662
01:27:06,014 --> 01:27:09,563
He tortures my father on the road,
without mercy.

663
01:27:10,356 --> 01:27:14,899
He spills the blood of my father, who is
the most merciful man on this earth.

664
01:27:15,590 --> 01:27:18,895
Until Savcı comes. He comes and saves
my father. Brings him home.

665
01:27:18,895 --> 01:27:21,325
And becomes my hero.

666
01:27:24,025 --> 01:27:28,356
As my father told me about his bravery,
I fell in love with him.

667
01:27:31,647 --> 01:27:34,894
How did you make brother Savcı
fall in love with you?

668
01:27:39,825 --> 01:27:41,590
With the name of Allah.

669
01:27:43,164 --> 01:27:47,941
With the 99 names of Allah...

670
01:27:49,004 --> 01:27:54,015
...who creates everything, who fills our
hearts with faith.

671
01:27:56,517 --> 01:27:58,485
My beys.

672
01:27:59,906 --> 01:28:02,609
-May Allah bless our council.
-Thank you.

673
01:28:09,804 --> 01:28:12,692
Because of the plague in Söğüt...

674
01:28:13,166 --> 01:28:16,187
...Dündar Bey assigned his authority
to Gündüz Bey.

675
01:28:16,187 --> 01:28:17,330
It's appropriate.

676
01:28:19,077 --> 01:28:22,812
As you ordered, my bey.
These are the decisions to take.

677
01:28:55,027 --> 01:28:56,297
My beys.

678
01:28:57,774 --> 01:29:01,519
This council is the council of
mind and heart.

679
01:29:03,153 --> 01:29:09,007
We were one, we emigrated, we conquered
and we became a thousand.

680
01:29:10,340 --> 01:29:12,950
We obtained castles, realms.

681
01:29:13,854 --> 01:29:16,424
Meanwhile...

682
01:29:17,572 --> 01:29:20,387
...our valiants took lives...

683
01:29:21,084 --> 01:29:22,544
...and lost their lives.

684
01:29:23,800 --> 01:29:28,595
But we saw that a strong
sword isn't enough...

685
01:29:31,439 --> 01:29:34,154
...the mind should be at least as sharp.

686
01:29:38,508 --> 01:29:40,489
Osman, my child...

687
01:29:41,395 --> 01:29:43,950
...may you live long.

688
01:29:46,493 --> 01:29:52,405
With both your sword and your mind,
you protected our Tents from Mongols.

689
01:29:53,558 --> 01:29:56,982
You conquered important places.

690
01:29:57,871 --> 01:30:02,658
But gaining victories don't matter,
preserving it does.

691
01:30:05,645 --> 01:30:07,811
If we don't organize well...

692
01:30:08,334 --> 01:30:11,077
...we will be ruined.
-Well said, my bey.

693
01:30:15,518 --> 01:30:20,632
For this reason, I commend Kuluca Hisar
to my son, Gündüz.

694
01:30:31,287 --> 01:30:33,854
I am happy and honored.

695
01:30:41,250 --> 01:30:46,020
If I betray the fiduciary, may I sacrifice
my life for the sword of justice.

696
01:30:46,657 --> 01:30:50,789
Thank you, my bey. Thank you, my bey.
-Thank you.

697
01:31:02,250 --> 01:31:05,270
Dündar Bey is appointed to Söğüt.

698
01:31:05,621 --> 01:31:07,997
He is afflicted with the plague.

699
01:31:09,421 --> 01:31:12,001
No one from the Tents
will go there.

700
01:31:25,238 --> 01:31:29,733
And the leader of our Alps will
be my son...

701
01:31:30,494 --> 01:31:32,940
May I enter, my Bey?

702
01:31:37,286 --> 01:31:39,861
Come, son.

703
01:31:59,532 --> 01:32:01,084
Brother.

704
01:32:24,152 --> 01:32:26,282
Where were you when these
men got murdered?

705
01:32:27,233 --> 01:32:31,086
Answer me, soldier! Where were you
when these men got murdered?

706
01:32:35,554 --> 01:32:38,206
How did they enter the castle, huh?

707
01:32:38,725 --> 01:32:40,978
How did they enter the castle?

708
01:32:41,663 --> 01:32:45,604
Answer me! How did they enter the castle?

709
01:32:50,527 --> 01:32:52,892
Where was your sentry post, huh?

710
01:32:53,982 --> 01:32:56,785
Answer me!
Get up!

711
01:32:57,495 --> 01:32:59,726
Get up!

712
01:33:00,871 --> 01:33:04,624
My father died in Karacahisar Castle
because of bumblers like you!

713
01:33:07,147 --> 01:33:09,999
I will kill you all!
I will kill you all!

714
01:33:11,550 --> 01:33:13,999
Vladius!

715
01:33:29,374 --> 01:33:30,880
Keep calm, my dear friend.

716
01:33:31,349 --> 01:33:32,747
Keep calm.

717
01:33:57,861 --> 01:34:00,075
They were my best men, Nicola.

718
01:34:01,815 --> 01:34:03,835
They died because of these bumblers.

719
01:34:05,111 --> 01:34:08,561
Your job isn't only protecting
this castle...

720
01:34:09,184 --> 01:34:11,730
...these stone walls.

721
01:34:15,994 --> 01:34:20,209
You protect our honor, dignity...

722
01:34:21,878 --> 01:34:24,065
...reputation.

723
01:34:25,915 --> 01:34:28,673
A simple mistake you will make...

724
01:34:31,543 --> 01:34:36,461
...will ruin the future of our children.

725
01:34:48,068 --> 01:34:51,719
-Are you the watch officer?
-Yes, sir.

726
01:34:55,181 --> 01:34:58,342
-Didn't you hear anything?
-No, sir.

727
01:35:03,934 --> 01:35:07,368
-Didn't you see anything?
-No, sir.

728
01:35:16,055 --> 01:35:19,601
I like caution.

729
01:35:52,677 --> 01:35:55,392
You will see it.

730
01:35:57,743 --> 01:36:00,408
You will see it.

731
01:36:12,055 --> 01:36:14,039
You will hear it.

732
01:36:25,628 --> 01:36:27,788
I will kill whoever did this, Nicola.

733
01:36:28,176 --> 01:36:31,632
We will find them, Vladius.
We will find them.

734
01:36:33,048 --> 01:36:35,133
We took our revenge, my Bey father.

735
01:36:36,286 --> 01:36:39,196
An eye for an eye and a tooth for a tooth.

736
01:36:41,946 --> 01:36:43,395
My beys..

737
01:36:44,709 --> 01:36:47,258
...they will pay with a thousand for
a life they take.

738
01:36:52,560 --> 01:36:54,496
My brother came from a campaign.

739
01:36:55,727 --> 01:36:59,572
What campaign is this? Let us know
so we can share the happiness.

740
01:37:01,445 --> 01:37:04,563
We killed Nicola's men who raided
us at Söğüt.

741
01:37:10,035 --> 01:37:11,985
Except for Vladius.

742
01:37:18,567 --> 01:37:20,463
Thank Allah.

743
01:37:22,224 --> 01:37:24,180
May Allah bless your holy war, brother.

744
01:37:27,836 --> 01:37:29,365
Thank you, brother.

745
01:37:31,919 --> 01:37:35,179
Long live, Savcı Bey.
You rose onto us like the sun.

746
01:37:42,509 --> 01:37:43,981
My beys.

747
01:37:45,890 --> 01:37:48,543
First Alp of our Tents will be...

748
01:38:02,183 --> 01:38:05,441
...my son, Savcı.

749
01:38:49,457 --> 01:38:51,578
May Allah help us, my Bey.

750
01:38:54,140 --> 01:38:55,770
Amin.

751
01:39:11,107 --> 01:39:13,676
- I congratulate you, brother.
- Thank you, brother.

752
01:39:14,870 --> 01:39:18,015
I want to hear about the Alps
after the council.

753
01:39:20,552 --> 01:39:22,408
Of course.

754
01:39:39,280 --> 01:39:40,823
Amin.

755
01:39:43,636 --> 01:39:49,985
O' Allah, make our Tents, our people
victorious.

756
01:39:53,007 --> 01:39:57,721
Don't leave us alone with our conceit,
with our desires.

757
01:40:00,328 --> 01:40:01,918
- Amin.
- Al-fatihah.

758
01:40:30,160 --> 01:40:31,902
Brother.

759
01:40:36,347 --> 01:40:37,785
Brother, welcome.

760
01:40:40,153 --> 01:40:41,376
Thank you.

761
01:40:51,649 --> 01:40:53,217
- Brother.
- Brother.

762
01:41:09,328 --> 01:41:11,176
Come with me, Savcı.

763
01:42:55,626 --> 01:42:58,873
It would deeply sorrow me to...

764
01:42:59,190 --> 01:43:01,757
..not be able to with him
while my brother..

765
01:43:02,693 --> 01:43:07,929
...Argun Khan was sleeping.

766
01:43:11,591 --> 01:43:20,387
But now, I see how painful his
death will be.

767
01:43:23,065 --> 01:43:27,086
- This is nothing, sir.
- Go on, tell me!

768
01:43:27,866 --> 01:43:30,404
Tell me more!

769
01:43:31,639 --> 01:43:34,758
- Tell me!
- The poison...

770
01:43:34,770 --> 01:43:41,340
...will tear his body as if he swallowed
thousand thorns.

771
01:43:42,281 --> 01:43:46,934
Like this rebellious Turkish Bey,
his eyes bleed first...

772
01:43:48,205 --> 01:43:53,269
...he will lose his skin,
his bones will be visible.

773
01:43:54,162 --> 01:43:57,000
But he won't die.

774
01:43:57,955 --> 01:44:00,253
Good.

775
01:44:03,423 --> 01:44:11,900
My brother's death shouldn't be as
easy as this Turk's.

776
01:44:13,040 --> 01:44:17,847
It should take months.
Maybe years.

777
01:44:21,590 --> 01:44:29,044
Until I sway all the kurultai beys to
my cause...

778
01:44:29,558 --> 01:44:33,829
...his death should be slow and painful.

779
01:44:54,578 --> 01:45:01,657
Before Argun dies, I should see his
demon face.

780
01:45:01,657 --> 01:45:07,055
I should mock the hatred on his eyes.

781
01:45:07,055 --> 01:45:12,100
Then, my nephew's turn will come.

782
01:45:16,614 --> 01:45:19,951
This won't be that easy, sir.

783
01:45:31,373 --> 01:45:35,024
When the Khagan gets elected...

784
01:45:35,885 --> 01:45:40,683
...I will buy all the Kurultai members,
one by one.

785
01:45:41,428 --> 01:45:46,779
There is no door that can't be opened
with gold.

786
01:45:47,594 --> 01:45:52,664
Mongol kurultai members, they
are all grasping.

787
01:45:53,612 --> 01:45:56,651
It's very difficult to give
them enough gold, sir.

788
01:45:57,474 --> 01:46:00,360
If the Seljuk treasury isn't enough...

789
01:46:01,047 --> 01:46:03,615
...there are Turkish tribes...

790
01:46:04,594 --> 01:46:08,290
...if that's not enough either,
the Christians.

791
01:46:09,330 --> 01:46:13,718
I will gather the bribe money
to become tha khagan...

792
01:46:14,149 --> 01:46:16,547
...from them.

793
01:46:18,177 --> 01:46:20,746
But that means more taxes, sir.

794
01:46:31,548 --> 01:46:35,216
Cerkutay begged to see you, Geyhatu.

795
01:46:36,541 --> 01:46:38,535
Bring him.

796
01:47:27,527 --> 01:47:29,799
İnegöl Castle

797
01:47:43,929 --> 01:47:48,145
I'm sure that the Kayıs have a spy
in the castle.

798
01:47:51,051 --> 01:47:53,497
First, they raided our ammunation...

799
01:47:53,891 --> 01:47:57,800
...then they came and killed the soldiers
I raided Söğüt with.

800
01:47:59,953 --> 01:48:03,123
Osman wasn't involved with either of them.

801
01:48:05,405 --> 01:48:08,526
Who do you think Ertuğrul asigned
for this?

802
01:48:10,186 --> 01:48:12,683
Gündüz?

803
01:48:13,756 --> 01:48:15,873
Or Dündar?

804
01:48:16,532 --> 01:48:17,998
Who?

805
01:48:20,121 --> 01:48:22,666
Neither of them are capable.

806
01:48:25,520 --> 01:48:27,184
Savcı.

807
01:48:28,354 --> 01:48:30,298
Savcı, huh?

808
01:48:32,900 --> 01:48:34,939
Why did you laugh?

809
01:48:35,269 --> 01:48:38,579
Two sons of Ertuğrul who are candidate
of taking his throne.

810
01:48:39,651 --> 01:48:42,440
Two pain in the neck.

811
01:48:45,465 --> 01:48:48,032
Osman has no chance against Savcı.

812
01:48:49,378 --> 01:48:52,376
Savcı is closer to the throne
in Ertuğrul's eyes.

813
01:48:55,151 --> 01:48:57,681
You are wrong, Vladius.

814
01:49:01,068 --> 01:49:03,897
Osman has something that Savcı don't have.

815
01:49:07,575 --> 01:49:09,546
What is it?

816
01:49:09,872 --> 01:49:14,096
You will find out. You will find out
when you find the spy.

817
01:49:18,433 --> 01:49:21,421
Vladius, civilian or soldier...

818
01:49:22,395 --> 01:49:26,352
...gain information about everyone
in the castle.

819
01:49:27,611 --> 01:49:34,134
I know only one thing about the spy.
He was here long before Ertuğrul's sons.

820
01:49:40,591 --> 01:49:43,589
- Who may that be?
- We'll find out.

821
01:49:45,133 --> 01:49:51,889
I will train the soldiers personally.
I will taught them personally.

822
01:49:53,640 --> 01:50:00,122
The war is on our doors.
The war is on our doors, Vladius.

823
01:50:11,810 --> 01:50:14,239
Cerkutay, Balgay's dog.

824
01:50:16,882 --> 01:50:20,426
So, you came here knowing that
you would die.

825
01:50:20,426 --> 01:50:23,854
I came here to die honorably
by your hands.

826
01:50:42,345 --> 01:50:45,000
Then...

827
01:50:49,282 --> 01:50:52,638
- Die!
- For one last time, for one last time...

828
01:50:52,638 --> 01:50:58,491
...allow me to serve you. Allow me to give
you an information more valuable than...

829
01:50:58,491 --> 01:51:00,910
...my life.

830
01:51:13,675 --> 01:51:16,256
More valuable than...

831
01:51:16,916 --> 01:51:19,198
...your life, huh?

832
01:51:26,055 --> 01:51:28,822
It's more valuable than your life
as well, Geyhatu.

833
01:51:29,752 --> 01:51:32,745
More valuable than my life, huh?

834
01:51:33,564 --> 01:51:35,302
What is it?

835
01:51:37,889 --> 01:51:39,968
Your son, Möngke.

836
01:51:43,266 --> 01:51:45,826
What happened to me son, speak!

837
01:51:46,573 --> 01:51:49,976
Osman! He killed your warriors and
abducted Möngke.

838
01:52:13,039 --> 01:52:16,916
I was wrong to look down on Osman.

839
01:52:17,748 --> 01:52:24,418
I won't let my son pay the price with
his glory.

840
01:52:44,548 --> 01:52:47,100
He won't kill Möngke.

841
01:52:55,396 --> 01:52:57,975
How do you know?

842
01:52:58,377 --> 01:53:03,139
He abducted Möngke because he is afraid
of your wroth. That's what I think.

843
01:53:05,277 --> 01:53:10,016
My son isn't the matter...

844
01:53:11,144 --> 01:53:15,607
...it's about my honor.

845
01:53:15,807 --> 01:53:17,601
My honor!

846
01:53:21,132 --> 01:53:24,843
Dead or alive,...

847
01:53:24,843 --> 01:53:27,848
...my son can't give it back..

848
01:53:29,144 --> 01:53:32,556
Only Osman...

849
01:53:33,214 --> 01:53:37,280
If there is someone
who will give my honor back...

850
01:53:38,648 --> 01:53:42,612
...It's Osman.

851
01:53:45,257 --> 01:53:51,474
I will clean my honor with Osman's
and his family's blood.

852
01:53:53,024 --> 01:53:57,849
Allow me to come with you.
My honor can only be cleaned...

853
01:53:58,481 --> 01:54:01,132
...if I die for you.

854
01:54:12,319 --> 01:54:16,283
Put on some clothes worthy
of a commander...

855
01:54:16,849 --> 01:54:20,408
...who is under my command...

856
01:54:22,043 --> 01:54:25,399
...then, come.

857
01:55:27,922 --> 01:55:29,199
Osman Bey.

858
01:55:31,072 --> 01:55:32,474
Ahmed Alp.

859
01:55:39,370 --> 01:55:42,286
- Want to do a sword drill?
- Some other time.

860
01:55:45,160 --> 01:55:48,320
- Want to wrestle?
I'll show you my muscles.

861
01:55:49,129 --> 01:55:51,228
Tomorrow, Ahmed.

862
01:55:55,085 --> 01:55:57,400
Are you coming from Ertuğrul Bey's tent?

863
01:55:58,898 --> 01:56:00,595
Yes.

864
01:56:01,593 --> 01:56:02,647
Yes.

865
01:56:04,135 --> 01:56:05,517
Osman Bey.

866
01:56:08,333 --> 01:56:11,229
My father is dead.

867
01:56:33,546 --> 01:56:35,698
Ahmed Alp.

868
01:56:36,780 --> 01:56:41,131
Fathers never die, Ahmed.

869
01:56:43,445 --> 01:56:45,817
Don't you ever forget that.

870
01:56:47,933 --> 01:56:53,012
Like everlasting coal in the
hearts of their children...

871
01:56:55,152 --> 01:56:58,780
...they are always alive.

872
01:57:12,555 --> 01:57:14,668
Ahmed Alp.

873
01:57:29,237 --> 01:57:30,189
Osman.

874
01:57:37,688 --> 01:57:40,336
What happened to Osman Bey?
He seems mad.

875
01:57:41,090 --> 01:57:43,038
I hope nothing is wrong.

876
01:57:45,734 --> 01:57:48,279
I congratulate, Lena.

877
01:57:49,182 --> 01:57:53,981
You came and made a scene.

878
01:57:58,258 --> 01:58:00,239
What's wrong, Hazal Hatun?

879
01:58:02,237 --> 01:58:06,078
Of course. Ertuğrul Bey...

880
01:58:07,184 --> 01:58:10,446
...took the leadership of the Alps
from Osman...

881
01:58:11,242 --> 01:58:13,167
...and gave it to Savcı Bey.

882
01:58:18,188 --> 01:58:20,502
Savcı is working for his Tents.

883
01:58:20,667 --> 01:58:22,712
I'm sure he deserved it.

884
01:58:23,203 --> 01:58:27,712
What is a position's worth between
brothers, Hazal Hatun?

885
01:58:28,422 --> 01:58:32,141
Be careful, women.
Look after your men.

886
01:58:34,405 --> 01:58:38,197
We shouldn't bother with
brother fights at the Tents.

887
01:58:39,763 --> 01:58:43,043
We just found peace.

888
01:59:03,483 --> 01:59:07,041
Karayel, karayel...

889
01:59:08,773 --> 01:59:12,385
Telling a strong stream to not flow...

890
01:59:12,769 --> 01:59:16,376
Telling horses running on steppes
to stop...

891
01:59:17,648 --> 01:59:20,633
Telling the winds to not blow,
is it suitable?

892
01:59:21,432 --> 01:59:23,645
Isn't that a shame?

893
01:59:24,231 --> 01:59:29,057
Tell me, Karayel. Tell me.
Would the wind stop blowing?

894
01:59:30,392 --> 01:59:32,413
Would the horses stop?

895
01:59:33,205 --> 01:59:35,359
Would the streams not flow?

896
01:59:36,839 --> 01:59:39,000
Then, why do they tell me to stop?

897
01:59:40,463 --> 01:59:42,983
Then, why do they tell me to
be silent?

898
01:59:44,977 --> 01:59:47,097
Ah, Karayel, ah...

899
01:59:47,471 --> 01:59:51,406
I tear my heart out.
My heart is boiling...

900
01:59:52,718 --> 01:59:54,671
My Allah, give me patience.

901
01:59:55,764 --> 01:59:57,638
My Allah, give me patience.

902
02:00:29,284 --> 02:00:31,603
Are you all right?
Come.

903
02:00:31,603 --> 02:00:35,294
- Come, take a breath.
- I'm fine.

904
02:00:57,617 --> 02:00:59,869
The nausea increased recently.

905
02:01:00,505 --> 02:01:03,519
I believe I'm pregnant.

906
02:01:04,815 --> 02:01:07,479
Mashallah.
Mashallah.

907
02:01:09,160 --> 02:01:12,809
- Does Savcı Bey know it?
- Not yet.

908
02:01:13,673 --> 02:01:17,461
- He will be so happy.
- Wouldn't he. He always says that a man...

909
02:01:17,461 --> 02:01:20,161
...need many children to make
a reputation.

910
02:01:23,503 --> 02:01:28,667
- Lena.
- I'm coming, my bey.

911
02:01:32,702 --> 02:01:34,220
Thank you.

912
02:01:36,678 --> 02:01:38,289
Lena.

913
02:01:47,294 --> 02:01:48,968
Tell me, what is it?

914
02:01:49,705 --> 02:01:51,196
It's not that easy.

915
02:01:51,742 --> 02:01:54,750
- Why is that?
- You waited that long.

916
02:01:55,664 --> 02:01:57,487
I won't say it that easily.

917
02:02:02,095 --> 02:02:03,843
Put some effort.

918
02:02:05,302 --> 02:02:07,137
Look for cures if necessary.

919
02:02:07,677 --> 02:02:10,482
It's rumored by the people...

920
02:02:10,674 --> 02:02:13,561
...that Bala Hatun can't
have a baby.

921
02:02:13,814 --> 02:02:17,543
One day, they can get into Osman's
head.

922
02:02:17,919 --> 02:02:20,976
Men don't have much patience.

923
02:02:21,747 --> 02:02:26,211
One day, you might be sharing
your tent with another woman.

924
02:02:35,114 --> 02:02:38,764
- Will you tell me?
- I will.

925
02:02:39,402 --> 02:02:41,446
Tell me then.

926
02:02:42,656 --> 02:02:45,096
Come, sit. I'll tell you my secret.

927
02:02:46,689 --> 02:02:49,584
It's not appropriate to sit there.

928
02:02:50,329 --> 02:02:53,124
Why? Won't you sit there
when the time comes.

929
02:02:54,528 --> 02:03:00,266
No one can know that. First, it's up to
Allah, then to my father and the beys.

930
02:03:00,791 --> 02:03:05,433
You became the First Alp.
We both know what's next.

931
02:03:07,629 --> 02:03:09,671
Still, you shouldn't say that.

932
02:03:11,732 --> 02:03:17,284
You deserve the throne, in the eyes
of your father and the beys.

933
02:03:19,680 --> 02:03:22,906
Only you, Savcı.
Only you.

934
02:03:26,172 --> 02:03:28,142
Come, sit here.

935
02:03:28,932 --> 02:03:30,879
Come on, we are alone.

936
02:03:31,169 --> 02:03:32,601
Come on.

937
02:03:46,876 --> 02:03:49,131
Now, close your eyes.

938
02:04:07,551 --> 02:04:09,126
You may open them.

939
02:04:16,513 --> 02:04:17,898
Lena?

940
02:04:19,727 --> 02:04:21,599
Are you?

941
02:04:24,794 --> 02:04:28,343
When I was pregnant
for Bayhoca, you gifted me this.

942
02:04:30,017 --> 02:04:34,392
I never took it off and prayed every day
for a son.

943
02:04:36,877 --> 02:04:38,787
I will be praying again.

944
02:04:44,204 --> 02:04:50,177
We will have another child, Savcı.
Kayı Tents' future Bey will have another son.

945
02:04:52,071 --> 02:04:54,689
Thank Allah.

946
02:05:22,695 --> 02:05:24,314
Salam Alaikum.

947
02:05:25,341 --> 02:05:27,047
Alaikum Salam, brother.

948
02:05:29,575 --> 02:05:31,433
Come.

949
02:05:34,362 --> 02:05:36,633
I have things to do.
If you allow me.

950
02:05:52,857 --> 02:05:54,715
I wanted to talk about Nicola, brother.

951
02:05:56,163 --> 02:05:58,055
I'm listening, brother.

952
02:06:04,054 --> 02:06:06,651
He isn't behind the trap set against me.

953
02:06:08,347 --> 02:06:10,624
I wanted you to know.

954
02:06:10,624 --> 02:06:14,176
You speak like you don't know the
ammunition incident, brother.

955
02:06:14,558 --> 02:06:18,934
They were going to blow off everywhere.
He is the one who bought Yavlak Aslan's...

956
02:06:18,934 --> 02:06:20,754
...helper and set the trap for you.

957
02:06:22,858 --> 02:06:25,744
I'm not saying that Nicola's intentions
are pure.

958
02:06:26,030 --> 02:06:30,239
But, there is someone else behind Yavlak
Aslan's helper, Kuzgun.

959
02:06:39,031 --> 02:06:41,246
Why are you telling me this.

960
02:06:45,307 --> 02:06:47,139
You are the First Alp.

961
02:06:48,338 --> 02:06:50,312
I thought you could take measures.

962
02:06:51,038 --> 02:06:53,884
Do you think I need your counsel, Osman?

963
02:06:55,093 --> 02:06:57,228
Not at all, brother.

964
02:06:59,327 --> 02:07:02,380
Osman, listen, brother

965
02:07:03,031 --> 02:07:06,035
You are valiant.
You are a warrior.

966
02:07:08,204 --> 02:07:09,290
But...

967
02:07:10,179 --> 02:07:12,273
...everything you think isn't
true.

968
02:07:14,148 --> 02:07:17,043
The Tents had been through a lot
last year.

969
02:07:17,837 --> 02:07:21,654
You couldn't move together with my uncle,
with my brother Gündüz.

970
02:07:22,453 --> 02:07:26,743
You went your way and they
were deceived by the enemy.

971
02:07:30,076 --> 02:07:32,595
What is the truth, brother?

972
02:07:37,264 --> 02:07:43,094
Now, we are at the Tents.
Neither you will go your own way.

973
02:07:44,075 --> 02:07:48,003
Nor we will let the enemy
deceive us.

974
02:07:52,261 --> 02:07:56,207
If it wasn't for my struggle last year...

975
02:07:57,722 --> 02:08:00,045
...we wouldn't be talking at this
tent today, brother.

976
02:08:03,559 --> 02:08:07,114
The past is past and the present is
present.

977
02:08:08,814 --> 02:08:11,020
From now, everyone will know their places.

978
02:08:11,339 --> 02:08:15,483
Everyone will move when they are told to
move and stop when they are told to stop.

979
02:08:15,759 --> 02:08:20,310
- Who will decide on that, brother?
- My father, Ertuğrul.

980
02:08:20,310 --> 02:08:23,760
And your older brother, I.

981
02:08:30,970 --> 02:08:33,463
You got used to my father's position.

982
02:08:38,325 --> 02:08:40,994
The fur fits you so well.

983
02:08:46,792 --> 02:08:48,217
So well.

984
02:08:49,721 --> 02:08:51,339
Never.

985
02:08:54,036 --> 02:08:56,388
Never accuse me.

986
02:08:58,658 --> 02:09:00,701
Our eyes aren't on the fur.

987
02:09:07,299 --> 02:09:09,939
What I heard and saw is enough for me.

988
02:09:11,387 --> 02:09:14,224
Both the fur and the position were
loved my many.

989
02:09:15,653 --> 02:09:18,772
Those who sat with passion,
got up with disappointment.

990
02:09:23,192 --> 02:09:25,088
Good luck with that.

991
02:09:25,174 --> 02:09:27,707
- Take your hands off me, brother.
- Take it back.

992
02:09:27,707 --> 02:09:29,277
Take off your hands, brother.

993
02:09:29,836 --> 02:09:33,538
- Osman, I won't repeat myself.
- I told you to take off your hands, brother!

994
02:09:49,019 --> 02:09:50,749
Never hit me again!

995
02:09:50,881 --> 02:09:52,163
Know your place!

996
02:09:52,192 --> 02:09:56,046
- Take it back!
- I didn't say anything to take back.

997
02:10:38,279 --> 02:10:40,553
There will be blood, Davud brother.

998
02:10:42,173 --> 02:10:44,678
Thank Allah, Ertuğrul Bey isn't here.

999
02:11:11,738 --> 02:11:15,132
My lion brother! Mashallah to my valiant!

1000
02:11:16,230 --> 02:11:19,106
You are getting stronger every day!

1001
02:11:22,071 --> 02:11:24,417
My lion brother.
Long live!

1002
02:11:24,864 --> 02:11:26,672
Long live!

1003
02:11:45,206 --> 02:11:48,937
Savcı Bey, mashallah.
You got even stronger.

1004
02:12:00,689 --> 02:12:02,660
My lion brother.

1005
02:12:07,878 --> 02:12:11,774
My dear brother...
My dear...

1006
02:12:33,037 --> 02:12:35,567
The fight for the fur has fired up.

1007
02:12:36,637 --> 02:12:38,235
Long live!

1008
02:13:08,940 --> 02:13:10,903
Geyhatu...

1009
02:13:22,272 --> 02:13:25,812
- It doesn't lack salt, does it?
- What's this haste, my hanım?

1010
02:13:30,104 --> 02:13:32,418
We are preparing dinner for Ertuğrul Bey.

1011
02:13:33,233 --> 02:13:36,702
Women should turn the tent into
heaven with their meals.

1012
02:13:37,818 --> 02:13:40,314
Bala Hatun went missing while
preparing dinner.

1013
02:13:43,399 --> 02:13:46,075
If she is missing, why do you care?

1014
02:13:46,190 --> 02:13:48,562
Is it your job? Mind your own work.

1015
02:13:52,910 --> 02:13:54,934
I'm sorry, I'm late.

1016
02:13:56,231 --> 02:14:00,024
- I left all the trouble for you.
- What trouble, Bala Hatun?

1017
02:14:00,244 --> 02:14:04,225
- It's our duty.
- You just came.

1018
02:14:04,392 --> 02:14:08,775
- You are working before resting.
- I carried this tent's burden for years.

1019
02:14:09,459 --> 02:14:11,701
Be at ease.

1020
02:14:16,100 --> 02:14:19,603
How is Osman Bey?
Did he calm down?

1021
02:14:20,394 --> 02:14:22,889
Osman Bey is in a good mood.

1022
02:14:23,134 --> 02:14:26,090
He will take care of the Tent's
affairs and rest for a while.

1023
02:14:26,682 --> 02:14:30,599
Last year, my valiant couldn't sleep
because of running one battle after another.

1024
02:14:32,446 --> 02:14:35,068
Thank Allah.

1025
02:15:16,643 --> 02:15:18,688
The dinner is ready, my Bey.

1026
02:15:22,913 --> 02:15:25,266
May Allah bless your hands, girls.

1027
02:15:29,900 --> 02:15:32,019
With the name of Allah.

1028
02:15:39,155 --> 02:15:40,968
Enjoy your meal.

1029
02:15:42,114 --> 02:15:43,797
With the name of Allah.

1030
02:15:56,351 --> 02:15:58,124
What's up?

1031
02:15:58,848 --> 02:16:05,964
You stopped the spread of the plague
in Söğüt. Is this why you are happy?

1032
02:16:07,484 --> 02:16:11,831
We are receiving good news from
both Söğüt and İnegöl Castle.

1033
02:16:13,072 --> 02:16:16,819
My nephew, Savcı, hit a severe
blow to the castle.

1034
02:16:17,386 --> 02:16:20,757
The echo of his slap
is still there, they say.

1035
02:16:20,929 --> 02:16:24,539
Sounds of whippings didn't end
until morning in the castle.

1036
02:16:25,691 --> 02:16:28,117
Nicole went mad with anger.

1037
02:16:37,305 --> 02:16:40,127
First Alp, my valiant son, Savcı.

1038
02:16:41,211 --> 02:16:45,159
You gave Nicola a good lesson.

1039
02:16:46,157 --> 02:16:49,510
When Nicola plans cunningness...

1040
02:16:50,026 --> 02:16:52,338
...he will think more than twice now.

1041
02:16:53,296 --> 02:16:58,088
Thank Allah, our Tents are in good
hands now.

1042
02:16:59,926 --> 02:17:05,541
Ertuğrul Bey is leading us.
Our beys are...

1043
02:17:05,541 --> 02:17:08,561
...doing their jobs.

1044
02:17:14,433 --> 02:17:22,739
Now, everyone should work harder than
ever before.

1045
02:17:24,659 --> 02:17:27,126
Not only beys or Alps...

1046
02:17:27,976 --> 02:17:30,004
...women too.

1047
02:17:33,580 --> 02:17:35,447
As you order, my bey.

1048
02:17:35,597 --> 02:17:38,375
- As you order, my bey.
- As you order, my bey.

1049
02:17:39,915 --> 02:17:44,052
What's wrong, my Bey father?
What is it that you know and we don't?

1050
02:17:46,804 --> 02:17:51,518
I heard that Geyhatu is on his
way with his army.

1051
02:18:00,621 --> 02:18:05,144
They say that he is coming to
raze Söğüt to ground...

1052
02:18:05,633 --> 02:18:08,093
...exterminate the Kayıs.

1053
02:18:08,749 --> 02:18:13,758
In a few days, the songs of
the birds won't be heard...

1054
02:18:13,903 --> 02:18:17,700
...because of the horses of
their warriors.

1055
02:18:17,993 --> 02:18:23,267
We know how to stop Geyhatu as we
stopped Balgay and Subutay before.

1056
02:18:24,861 --> 02:18:27,575
It's time to keep valiantness on its
sheath...

1057
02:18:27,575 --> 02:18:30,976
...until the right time comes, Osman.

1058
02:18:33,680 --> 02:18:35,175
Hence...

1059
02:18:35,465 --> 02:18:38,920
...we need to send a messenger
to Gethatu...

1060
02:18:38,920 --> 02:18:41,220
...whose tongue is as sharp as
his blade.

1061
02:18:44,535 --> 02:18:48,903
If you allow me, I apply for the mission.

1062
02:19:05,139 --> 02:19:08,762
I know that all the beys here...

1063
02:19:09,114 --> 02:19:14,007
...would do this mission without fear.

1064
02:19:16,896 --> 02:19:20,945
But I will give this mission
to Savcı.

1065
02:19:34,272 --> 02:19:37,257
Before sunrise, go swiftly, Savcı.

1066
02:19:37,990 --> 02:19:40,098
As you order, my bey.